  "summary": "I am a software engineer and love to program. My strongest languages are C++ and D, and in my free time, I am one of the maintainers of D's standard library. I am the author the date/time solution in D's standard library. I was sick of time-related bugs at work, so when D needed a new date/time solution, I was very well informed (and quite opinionated) about what a proper date/time solution should look like, and I stepped up to implemented it for D's standard library. I have done a lot of other work on D's standard library since. I've also worked on a number of personal projects, but very few are currently available online. Ialso have experience in a variety of other programming languages such as Java and Haskell.\n\nI care a great deal about writing high quality code and strongly believe in techniques such as unit testing and using valgrind to make sure that your code does the right thing and continues to do the right thing as it's refactored.",
